   │        -------------------- `parsed` is checked here
   ·
18 │       let assert Ok(value) = parsed
   │       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `parsed` was already checked, so this assert can't fail

Gleam's conventions call checking a value and then asserting its shape an
anti-pattern that "should never be done". The check and the assert can
drift apart as the code changes.

